<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Scimitar</h1>
<p>Also referred to as the scymitar and scimiter. The scimitar is a Middle Eastern sword characterized by a broad, curved blade ending in a uniquely upturned point. While most associate a scimitar with the broad-bladed weapons popularized by the Tales of Sinbad, many scimitars were actually rather narrow-bladed weapons along the lines of shamshirs or talwars.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the scimitar is a weapon skill of its own, one of the swords (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): one-handed, it slashes, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is of middling speed. It is taught by the fighters from guild level 4, the knights from guild level 4, the paladins from guild level 4 and the thieves from guild level 12 (up to 80%).
</p><p><br />
